// The other half of a two-file program (v0.23.13-dev, P3.4).
//
// Before `include` existed, the two lines below had to be typed here by hand —
// and nothing checked them against the definitions in include_demo_defs.ast.
// The linker matches by name, so a retyped arity or return type linked, ran,
// and returned garbage silently. Now the declaration comes from the file that
// holds the body, so it cannot disagree with it.
//
// What crosses an include is declarations only: `add2`'s body and `total`'s
// initializer stay in include_demo_defs.ast, which is compiled separately.
//
//   aster build-obj examples/include_demo_defs.ast -o defs.o
//   aster build-obj examples/include_demo_main.ast -o main.o
//   aster link-obj main.o defs.o -o demo && ./demo   # prints 9
//
// The path is relative to *this* file, not to the working directory, so the
// three commands work from anywhere.

include "include_demo_defs.ast";

fn main() -> i32 {
    return add2(total);
}
